SCENE: Night, harbor warehouse. Spanner Girl sits against the closed End B wall, RIGHT lower shin/boot pinned by the bottom edge of an upright white boat at her RIGHT (screen-LEFT). Boss holds a 100-ton ship overhead 12.5 m away. She catches her wrench, throws it straight back; its horizontal jaw clamps his LEFT lower shin. She twists it remotely; he collapses, the ship drops, the shock topples the white boat off her RIGHT leg before dust fills the over-the-shoulder (O/S) frame.

REFERENCES:
@image1: warehouse, parallel boat racks, concrete, trusses, practical lights.
@image2: closed corrugated End B wall behind her.
@image3: Spanner Girl and wrench. Adult face, black bob, red top/gloves, mustard trousers, boots. One worn silver 180 cm, 200 kg wrench: broad open C-shaped adjustable jaw, thick shaft, rounded handle. Bright young adult Korean female exertion voice. Match exactly.
@image4: Boss, 2.10 m adult, sunglasses, black suit/shoes; assistance housings stay around his arms and hands. Deep, rough, chest-resonant voice. Match exactly.
@image5: 3.5 m, one-ton rusty white motorboat, damaged glazing, exposed cockpit. Match exactly.
@image6: 100-ton rusted ship, 15.75 m (7.5 Boss-heights); keep hull, wheelhouse, mast, crane, hook. Both his hands support its underside; bow faces her.
@image7: POSITION DIAGRAM ONLY (mint=Boss, red=Girl, yellow=white boat, blue=wrench). Colored marks never appear in footage.
@image8: PREVIOUS-STATE position/contact reference only: seated pose, white boat at her RIGHT, RIGHT boot/lower-shin pinning. Its framing sets no camera; gray face-cover annotation not filmed; face/costume from @image3 only.

LOCATION: 50 m aisle ends at her End B wall; Boss 12.5 m away. She sits, buttocks on floor, legs forward; boat's upper hull touches the wall; its edge presses her RIGHT shin/boot onto concrete (compressed trouser, contact shadow). LEFT leg and arms free; hips grounded. Boss: LEFT foot half-step forward, RIGHT knee on broken concrete, already pushing up. Keep RIGHT bank of A-B axis; Boss camera on his RIGHT-front, 25 deg off frontal. O/S keeps Girl and boat RIGHT, Boss and ship LEFT.
WRENCH: one rigid 180 cm tool, RIGHT-hand catch and immediate throw, no twirl. At the clamp, head and shaft lie horizontal at lower-shin height; never upright. Camera has weight and braking.

FORMAT: 14.000 s, 336 frames, 21:9, 24 fps, five real-time shots, hard cuts only at 1.5, 4.5, 5.5, 9.0 s. End in Shot 5's near-black dust at 14.0 s. No slow motion or ramps.

SHOT 1 (0.0-1.5): Near-frontal bust-to-waist, face center-right, large soft RIGHT glove in left foreground, urgent eyes on wrench, legs below frame. 0.0-0.3: wrench flies at 130 km/h from camera-side aisle, handle-first, jaw trailing, into her RIGHT hand; arm nearly pulled straight, hips planted. 0.3-1.15: no pause, one pull-and-drive of the same arm throws it back. 1.15-1.5: forceful release, loud "하!", wrench jaw-first at 90 km/h, horizontal, sweeps past lens.
CUT 1.5
SHOT 2 (1.5-4.5): 63-deg very low diagonal FULL SHOT, camera ~20 cm above broken floor, 25 deg toward Boss's RIGHT, looking sharply up: both shoes, whole body, huge hull at top. First ~0.4 s he finishes standing, already roaring, arms trembling; slabs sink with a crunch, powder jets; he catches the lagging hull, lockout overhead. Then ONE continuous joyful victory roar. During it, ~0.5 s after the throw, the wrench arrives LYING HORIZONTALLY, open C jaw aligned with his LEFT lower shin above the ankle, shaft sideways low above floor. Shin enters the opening, jaw faces in front of and behind the leg; heavy CLACK; shadows show the grip; foot stays planted. Wrench stays locked till Shot 5 twist. Rack focus to jaw/shin.
CUT 4.5
SHOT 3 (4.5-5.5): 12-deg facial extreme close-up, same low 25-deg diagonal; sunglasses, sweat. He dips chin to the wrench, brow creases in alarm, then sharply looks toward Spanner Girl, realizing; heavy breath, low growl, mouth slightly open.
CUT 5.5
SHOT 4 (5.5-9.0): 47-deg near-frontal physical push-in to BUST with face and BOTH hands; same upright white hull beside her, corrugated wall; right leg pinned below frame. Lamps flicker; grit sifts. She brings both red-gloved hands under chin and INTERLACES fingers in one firm clasp, elbows bent; fingers stay interlaced throughout. Looks above the lens at Boss, one mouth corner up: confident, slightly sadistic delight. Push-in done by 7.85 s, hold ~0.7 s. At ~8.6 s she releases ONE louder full-chested "하아아아앗!" (~0.8 s, carries across the cut) driving CLASPED hands straight forward, palms outward. Hold this pose continuously across the cut through 14.0 s.
CUT 9.0
SHOT 5 (9.0-14.0): 84-deg TRUE REAR O/S, same camera bank, farther back, full seated body: Girl RIGHT, hips and both legs in frame, white boat lower-right, RIGHT shin/boot trapped under it visible; Focus on Boss and ship in LEFT middle distance; keep framing throughout. 9.0-9.5: after her extension, the locked wrench makes ONE constrained ~180-deg half-turn, turning his LEFT ankle and boot with it, then HARD STOP and hold; no full revolution, spin or back-and-forth. Dry "우두둑" crunch; ankle stays attached; knee buckles; ~0.5 s balance struggle. ~9.5 s: ONE long, extremely loud, thin high pain scream, sustained unbroken through the fall until the hull lands. Grip fails: torso pitches FORWARD, one palm slips. By ~10.3 s he falls on his front; ship rises briefly clear of his hands, then drops heavily. Keel punches concrete ~11.0 s, floor collapses over 1 m deep, fissures race. His scream is cut off by the impact (only his voice); crash stays full. Sonic-boom CRACK; handheld camera jolts and rolls violently, regains the same O/S. Impact knocks the jaw free of the ankle; wrench slides sideways, lost in dust. Warehouse shudders: lamps whip, debris falls, ALL stored boats knock, some topple. Floor dust precedes the thick cloud, reaching the white boat: the ENTIRE boat heaves clear of the floor in ONE LARGE HEAVE with a visible gap over her RIGHT shin/boot, rolls OUTWARD and fully topples on its outer side with a hollow metal crash. Her RIGHT boot is exposed, she draws the heel back; readable ~0.4 s before opaque dust. Only then thick dust arrives; she keeps the extended pose. By 13.5 s ~90% near-black dust covers her whole figure, held to 14.0 s; no further cut.

LIGHT/AUDIO: Fixed 4200K low-key, practicals; exposure fixed. 30-40% haze Shots 1-4. Sound: heavy catch, throw cry, Boss's single roar, CLACK, "하아아아앗!", one "우두둑", one long thin scream, crash, racks, toppling boats, boat overturn, electrical sputter. No music. No subtitles.

LOCKS: Her RIGHT foot pinned until impact; wrench never completes a full revolution; scream ends under the ship; white boat fully topples, freeing her RIGHT leg before near-black dust.

15 SECONDS, STRICTLY 10 SHOTS, HARD CUTS AT 1.5, 3, 4.5, 6, 7.5, 9, 10.5, 12, 13.5 s, REAL-TIME SPEED. Black arena at night, extreme close-ups: each fighter spins and twirls their own weapon with show-off ease, hand and weapon filling the frame, face only a blurred edge. Then Leo: his mechanical arm, then his sneakers. Each cut lands on the move.
WHO IS WHO (each reference is the only source of that look)
@char_az2_lordanus_v1 = Lord Anus: HOOD ALWAYS UP, silver gloves with long hooked claws, black smoke. His weapons are his claws.
@char_az1_monsterwarrior_v1 = Hammerhead: shark monster, dark blue scales.
@prop_az1_ring-chakram = Hammerhead's ring, his only weapon; he holds it still by the bar across its middle; it never spins.
@char_az1_girlwarrior_v1 = the Necromancer: small pale blue-violet girl. No wings.
@prop_az1_hammer-girl-warrior = the Necromancer's hammer, light in her hands.
@v_char_az2_cicada_elia2_torn_v1 = ELIA: BLACK shoulder-length hair, one wing TORN. Weapon @prop_cicada-rifle-elia-2_v1 : revolver with a blade under the barrel, right hand.
@v_char_az2_cicada_eli3_armed_short = ELI: bright RED hair combed back, wings whole. Weapon @prop_cicada-glaive-eli-1_v1 : ONE super-long black sword, right hand.
@v_char_az2_cicada_el1_armed_short = EL: messy short SILVER-WHITE hair, wings whole. Weapons @prop_cicada-blades-el-3_v1 : one blade in each fist.
The sisters share one shell suit and dragonfly wings; hair colour and weapon tell them apart. Each weapon comes only from its own reference, keeps its shape in every frame and stays with its owner.
@v_char_az2_nisa_v2_short = Nisa Weapons @prop_AZ2_NisaDaggers_v1 : two daggers, one per hand.
@char_az1_dogwarrior_v1 = the Dog Knight: white dog warrior on hind legs. Weapon @prop_az1_sword-dog-warrior : his long sword.
@v_char_az2_leo_v7_short = Leo, the only human His right arm is the mechanical arm @prop_AZ2_ScrapMechArm_v1 ; his left hand is his own. His sneakers throw green lightning.
@loc_az2_arena_black = the ONLY place: night, dark red sand, black rune walls, tiny warm crowd lights, black sky, knee-high red fog lighting fighters from below.
CAMERA: handheld wide lens one step from the bodies, moving from the first frame to the last of every shot, swaying with steps and breath, arriving a little late and landing back on the hand and weapon; still moving at every cut. Natural speed.
SHOT 1 0–1.5 s — Lord Anus @char_az2_lordanus_v1 lifts his hand and rolls his fingers in a slow wave, the hooked silver claws clicking one after another, black smoke curling between them; hood edge and pale chin blurred at the frame edge. Under his hand looking up through the claws at the black sky, frame tilted 25°, ~63° view; dips a palm's height toward the claws, then rises back late.
SHOT 2 1.5–3 s — The Necromancer @char_az1_girlwarrior_v1 spins her hammer @prop_az1_hammer-girl-warrior by the end of its handle in her fingers like a baton, the head whipping past, red lightning flicking off it. Close beside her spinning hand, handle wheeling past the lens, tilted 20° the other way, ~84° view; half a step in after her as she leans forward, late, landing on the handle in her fingers.
SHOT 3 3–4.5 s — Eli @v_char_az2_cicada_eli3_armed_short spins her super-long black sword @prop_cicada-glaive-eli-1_v1 round her wrist in a black arc, then catches the grip dead still; a strand of red hair crosses the frame. At her wrist looking along her forearm, ~63° view; drifts half a step sideways, landing on her grip.
SHOT 4 4.5–6 s — Hammerhead @char_az1_monsterwarrior_v1 tightens his huge scaled fist on the bar of his ring @prop_az1_ring-chakram , knuckles cracking, and tilts the ring slowly so its rim passes close by the lens; the ring does not turn. Close under his fist looking up past the rim, tilted 30°, ~84° view; drifts half a step sideways, landing on his fist on the bar.
SHOT 5 6–7.5 s — El @v_char_az2_cicada_el1_armed_short spins both blades @prop_cicada-blades-el-3_v1 in her fingers, flips them into reverse grip at the same instant and back, steel flashing; a strand of silver-white hair crosses the frame. Straight above her hands looking down, ~63° view; tilts up once to her wrists, late, and comes back, landing on the blades.
SHOT 6 7.5–9 s — The Dog Knight @char_az1_dogwarrior_v1 twirls his long sword @prop_az1_sword-dog-warrior in his paw, grip rolling through his fingers, cross guard flashing past, and stops it dead pointing down; white fur on the back of the paw. Behind his paw over his knuckles, tilted 15°, ~84° view; drifts half a step sideways, landing on his paw on the grip.
SHOT 7 9–10.5 s — Elia @v_char_az2_cicada_elia2_torn_v1 spins her revolver @prop_cicada-rifle-elia-2_v1 round her trigger finger, stops it dead in her palm, and her thumb cocks the hammer with a click; a strand of black hair at the edge. Beside the cylinder looking across her trigger finger and the under-barrel blade, tilted 20° the other way, ~63° view; drifts half a step sideways, landing on the revolver in her palm.
SHOT 8 10.5–12 s — Nisa @v_char_az2_nisa_v2_short tosses one dagger @prop_AZ2_NisaDaggers_v1 up, it flips once, and she catches it by the grip in a reverse hold, dead still; oxblood leather cuff. Low under her hand looking up, ~84° view; rises with her open palm to the falling dagger, arriving late, carrying past, landing on the dagger in her palm.
SHOT 9 12–13.5 s — Leo @v_char_az2_leo_v7_short opens his mechanical right hand @prop_AZ2_ScrapMechArm_v1 finger by finger, plates sliding, servos whirring, green sparks jumping between plates, then clenches a fist. Close in front of the opening palm, tilted 15°, ~63° view; drifts half a step sideways, landing on the mechanical fist.
SHOT 10 13.5–15 s — Leo @v_char_az2_leo_v7_short rubs the toe of one sneaker against the top-front of the other; green lightning crackles out of the soles and crawls over the dark red sand toward the lens. On the sand at his sneakers looking along the toes, tilted 25°, ~47° view; dips a palm's height toward the lightning, rises back late to the sneakers.
SOUND: distant crowd roar; close and loud on every shot: claws clicking, hammer whoosh and red lightning crackle, long sword whistle, knuckles cracking on the ring bar, two blades ringing, sword grip slapping into the paw, revolver cylinder whirring and hammer cocking, dagger landing in a palm, servos whirring, sneakers squeaking and green lightning crackling. No music, no talking.
RULES: exactly ten shots in this order: Lord Anus's claws, Necromancer's hammer, Eli's sword, Hammerhead's ring, El's blades, Dog Knight's sword, Elia's revolver, Nisa's dagger, Leo's mechanical arm, Leo's sneakers. Hammerhead's ring only gets gripped and tilted.
STYLE: live-action night fantasy, real weight, deep blacks, film grain.

FORMAT — Multishot: five shots, 25.0 s, four hard cuts at 0:04.0, 0:12.0, 0:17.0, 0:21.0. Real time; one rectilinear lens and one slow camera move per shot; zero cuts in shot 2.

AUDIO — SFX and speech only. No music of any kind: room tone, listed sounds, two voices; instruments: zero. Machine has no speaker: one soft click when the tips set, then a thin glassy whir, even to the end. Spoken words: six, each line once, lip-synced, unhurried: NISA in shot 3, LEO in shot 4; shots 1, 2, 5 no words.

REFERENCES — the pins set every look.
@v_char_az2_leo_v7_long — LEO: face, curly hair, moustache, build, costume 100%; RIGHT ARM pale metal prosthetic, left arm flesh; ignore studio. 185 cm.
@v_char_az2_nisa_v2_long — NISA: face, hair, skin, makeup, build, costume 100%; ignore studio. 183 cm.
@loc_az2_jukeboxroom_v2 — the chamber one to one (walls, walkway, platform, machine, light); keyframe of shot 1 only; its spheres drift in the clip. Ambient off.
@loc_az2_jukeboxroom_cu_v1 — the machine seen from the walkway's last planks, square to the plate: geography of machine shots; riveted deck opens RIGHT of the trunk (NISA's deck). Shot 3 is this camera closer and lower; shots 4–5 cut inside this space.
@prop_AZ2_Jukebox_v1 — the machine (~180 cm, two arms to thin tips, plate with blue and green lights) with the sphere seated, each tip touching the glass: pose and sphere place from the set to the end, sphere spinning, lit inside. Not its grey studio.
@prop_az2_jukebox_vinyl — the glass sphere, 20 cm, smaller than a head, fine etched rings, glitter inside: every sphere, and the chosen one.

CONTEXT — NISA has just pressed her planet in the machine's archive; a dark sphere below the walkway, THE CHOSEN SPHERE, will wake, fly to the machine, set and spin.

LOCKS — Exactly two people. LEO taller by half a head: top of her head at his eyes, her eyes at his mouth. Machine tips at top of NISA's head, plate at her hip, seated sphere at her chin. LEO on the walkway, two paces short of the platform, LEFT rail; NISA on the platform RIGHT of the trunk, facing camera and LEO, machine at her right side. LEO left, NISA right in every shot; shots 3–5 on shot 1's side of the line. LEO's steps: two, short; jumps over the rail: zero. Spheres: over a hundred, 20 cm, weightless, ALL drifting in one counter-clockwise current, 0.5 m/s, LEFT TO RIGHT on screen; spheres still or in the same frame place at a shot's first and last frame: zero. Three layers every shot: big soft sphere ~40 cm from lens drifting across the foreground (never the one touched), sharp middle, soft far spheres sliding right, ~8 s per frame width. Only the chosen sphere flies or glows; tips hold empty air until it arrives; after the set it spins about a vertical axis every frame — upper tip still on its pole, side tip riding the middle ring, flecks sweeping (one circuit per 2 s, then faster), one fixed highlight; light stays in the glass, beams: zero. Its path never touches the walkway. Eyes on lens: zero. Smiles: NISA one (shot 5), LEO one half-grin (shot 4); laughs: zero.

SHOT 1, 0:00.0–0:04.0 — THE WIDE, framing of @loc_az2_jukeboxroom_v2 plus the two, deep focus. LEO full figure, back to camera, head turning: ceiling 0:00.5, left wall 0:01.5, spheres right 0:02.5, her 0:03.5. NISA leans, right elbow on the machine's arm, watching him; tips empty. 0:00.5 soft near sphere crosses the lower frame. 0:01.0 a sphere passes behind LEO at shoulder height. 0:01.5 NISA flicks a sphere away with the back of her left hand without looking; it drifts on. Chosen sphere drifts dark below the walkway. Sound: air, a tap on glass. Camera glides 0.5 m LEFT.

SHOT 2, 0:04.0–0:12.0 — THE ONE-SHOT. 35 mm, wide aperture, focus locked on the sphere, background streaking. Chase camera 60 cm behind, sphere centred, a third of frame height. 0:04.0–0:05.0 dark sphere drifts with the current under the planks. 0:05.0–0:05.5 a warm point lights inside; still at current pace. 0:05.5–0:07.5 flight, 7 m/s, open air: back under the walkway, out on LEO's side, climbing U-turn over the drop, forward outside the left rail at knee height; LEO from behind, head up-left; it whips past; his left foot twitches, right foot planted; head follows; ONE STEP closer. NISA lifts her elbow, steps one pace screen-right, eyes on it — she saw it first. It rises past the plate. 0:07.5–0:08.5 slows into the gap at her chin height, tips draw back, stops dead; camera 70 cm away, sphere half frame height, pose of @prop_AZ2_Jukebox_v1; tips set on pole and middle ring — ONE SOFT CLICK. 0:08.5–0:12.0 spins; orange-gold point grows to white-gold by 0:11, lighting tips, arms and NISA's face at right. Camera pushes in 20 cm. Sound: air rush, LEO's startled breath, tips' metal whisper, click, whir and tick.

SHOT 3, 0:12.0–0:17.0 — FROM THE WALKWAY'S END. 35 mm, focus on NISA. Camera of @loc_az2_jukeboxroom_cu_v1 at 1.5 m from the trunk, plate height, tilted up. Spinning sphere upper left. 0:12.0–0:13.0 NISA strolls the deck screen-right, face up to the cloud. 0:13.0–0:14.5 fingertip on a passing sphere, eyes on it: "All that remains" — light; she stops. 0:14.5–0:16.0 eyes to LEO (left of and above lens), head tilts, eyebrow up: "is music." — softer. Full line once: "All that remains is music." 0:16.0–0:17.0 holds the look. A sphere crosses behind her head at 0:15.5. Camera dollies 0.5 m RIGHT with her.

SHOT 4, 0:17.0–0:21.0 — CLOSE ON LEO OVER NISA'S LEFT SHOULDER. 75 mm, wide open, focus on his eyes. Camera at her shoulder height, 2 m behind, looking up; her hair soft at right edge; his face above the horizon; bokeh sliding right. Eyebrow up, lazy half-grin, ONE LAZY HALF-STEP; breath of a laugh; at 0:19.0 "Music?" — light, sceptical, surprised underneath. Eyes to the sphere and back; grin thins to a puzzled half-frown. Camera glides 30 cm LEFT.

SHOT 5, 0:21.0–0:25.0 — OVER LEO'S RIGHT SHOULDER ONTO NISA. 75 mm, focus on NISA. Camera at his eye height, 1.5 m behind, looking down; his head and metal shoulder soft left third; NISA chest up, eyes below horizon; spinning sphere at left edge. 0:21.0–0:22.0 still. 0:22.0–0:23.0 hand on hip, playful head toss, small warm smile. 0:23.0–0:24.0 turns her back. 0:24.0–0:25.0 one step away; ends on her back. Sphere behind her head at 0:22.5. Camera glides 30 cm LEFT.

COLOUR — 70 violet walls in near-dark; 20 mauve walkway, platform, sphere glints; 10 machine lights and the orange-gold to white-gold sphere. Practical light, faint haze, no lettering.

STYLE — ARENA ZERO EP2: photorealistic live-action film image shot on anamorphic lenses, 2.39:1, shallow depth of field, oval bokeh, horizontal flares, subtle grain and halation, dust, sweat and pores, worn fabrics; practical sets and prosthetics; everything unbranded.
